```json
{
  "hooks": {
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "/Users/soph/.claude/title-stamp.sh"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

Then **restart Claude Code** (so it reloads settings), and in the fresh session just send me any short message. The hook will log to `/tmp/title-hook.log`, and I'll read it to see whether it fired, what tty it resolved, and whether the write succeeded — that'll pinpoint the actual failure. No need to watch the tab this round; the log is the diagnostic.

